1. **The key-sequence decoder** (`src/console/keys.rs`). Replace `Key::of` (one class per read, lines 21-29) with a
   `Decoder` the loop owns: `feed(bytes, now)` returns the keys a read completes, and `flush(now)` returns a lone ESC
   once 50 ms pass with nothing after it. The reader thread (`spawn`, lines 46-63) sends each read's bytes, still at
   most `READ_CAP` 64 (line 9). The classes are closed:
   - interrupt (0x03 anywhere in a read, as now), quit (`q`);
   - up (`\x1b[A`, `\x1bOA`, `k`), down (`\x1b[B`, `\x1bOB`, `j`);
   - enter (CR), escape (a lone ESC), backspace (0x7f, 0x08);
   - a printable char (an ASCII printable or one whole UTF-8 scalar, assembled across reads);
   - unbound (any other byte or sequence, a CSI or SS3 sequence read whole to its final byte).
   A sequence split across reads decodes as one key. The key's meaning (a verb letter, `y`/`n`, a typed char) is the
   loop's, by mode (step 4). No key byte reaches any line (keeps arch S5, obs S4). Unit cases in an rstest table,
   named `decoder_…`, inline (keeps tests S3).

6. **The five Part-1 verbs and the confirm** (`src/console/action.rs`, `src/console/mod.rs`). On the selected name:
   - `l` → `viola last <name>`;
   - `p` → `viola pause <name>`;
   - `f` → `viola focus <name>`;
   - `r` → the confirm `release <name>? y/n`, then `viola release <name>` on `y`;
   - `v` → the confirm `revive <name>? y/n`, then `viola up <name>` on `y`: a passed revive takes the terminal it runs
     in, and `up` re-opens a named instance in a terminal of its own (`src/cmd/up.rs:39-40`).
   Each verb's refusal is its own line, drawn as captured. No action runs with no selection.

10. **The editing line** (`src/console/mod.rs`, `src/human/console.rs`). An editing mode with its prompt on the key
    row:
    - printable chars append, backspace removes one, enter submits, escape cancels, interrupt ends the console;
    - `q` and the verb letters are text here;
    - a CR inside a read ends the line, and the rest of that read is dropped (one line per send, F4);
    - the line is bounded at `MAX_FRAME` bytes, and keys past the bound read `unbound`;
    - the drawn echo is the tail that fits the width, in Q9's answered form (its recommended arm: as typed, controls
      escaped).
    The text is handed unchanged: no trim, no rewrite (design-system `contract/send-readback/prompt`).

- (product) In Part 2, `s` sends the editing line through `viola send` and draws its mirror lines as its readback;
  `m` switches through `viola switch`; `o` opens a child through `viola open --parent`: the part-2 e2e filter green
  (matrix#v2-15's send and open legs; v2-31's console leg).

4. **The loop's modes** — built: `src/console/mod.rs`, `Mode` {`List`, `Confirm(Action)`} (line 144), `Shown`
   (line 151), `State` (line 159) with `view` (179), `press` (201), `list_key` (213), `confirm_key` (250), `reap` (294);
   `run` (line 326) feeds each read to the decoder and presses its keys one by one (lines 369-373).

10. **The editing mode** (`src/console/mod.rs`). `Mode` gains `Editing { verb, name, text }`, its prompt in the key
    line's place:
    - a `Char` appends its scalar, `Backspace` removes the last scalar, `Enter` submits, `Escape` cancels, `Interrupt`
      ends the console; `q`, `j`, `k` and the verb letters are text here (step 1's departure);
    - `Unbound` (a C0 byte, TAB included, a C1 scalar, a malformed UTF-8 sequence, an escape sequence) appends nothing;
    - the text is bounded at `MAX_FRAME` bytes, and a char past the bound appends nothing and counts as `unbound`;
    - `Enter`, `Escape` and `Interrupt` end the read's editing: the rest of that read is dropped, so a CR inside a
      paste ends the line (one line per send, F4);
    - the text is handed unchanged: no trim, no rewrite (design-system `contract/send-readback/prompt`).

- Rows: security-plan `decision/console-key-reader-bounded`, `decision/console-terminal-and-home-check`,
  `decision/console-agents-child-outlives-quit`, `decision/question-option-text-crosses-boundary`; architecture
  `decision/no-shell-out`, `decision/human-controls-cli-only`, `decision/option-text-never-in-human-line`;
  design-system `decision/list-is-the-board`, `contract/fleet-console-keys/unbound`,
  `contract/fleet-console-view/more-line`, `decision/escape-controls-in-human-output`, `contract/send-readback/prompt`;
  layout-templates `decision/board-vs-strip`, `decision/console-frame-floor`, `decision/console-own-surface`; obs-plan
  `contract/diag-line-fields/console-key`, `decision/codes-only-role-logs`, `decision/no-interactive-terminal-interface`,
  `decision/dialog-text-never-logged`; a11y-plan `decision/cli-no-interactive-input`, `decision/static-linear-output`;
  test-plan `decision/tests-never-read-host-sessions`, `decision/tui-verdicts-from-records`.
